            <p>
                Seasonal rituals remain central to cultural life. Ivana Kupala, a midsummer celebration rooted in ancient folklore,
                reflects the close relationship between nature, symbolism, and communal unity.
            </p>
            <p>
                Christmas traditions, the traditional carol “Shchedryk”, composed by Mykola Leontovych,
                later became known worldwide as “Carol of the Bells.” This transformation illustrates how Ukrainian cultural
                heritage has reached a global audience while maintaining its original roots.
            </p>
